<title>CANADA: Thunder Bay Harbour Commission April cargo stats.</title>
<headline>Thunder Bay Harbour Commission April cargo stats.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain and potash shipments out of Canada's Great Lakes port of Thunder Bay were 9.1 and 3.7 percent higher, respectively, in April compared to the same month last year while coal was down 22 percent, Thunder Bay Harbour Commission statistics show.</p>
<p>COMMODITY     APRIL '97 APRIL '96 APRIL '95</p>
<p>Grain	   822,756   753,973   891,944 Tonnes</p>
<p>Coal	     83,748   107,346   176,951 Tonnes</p>
<p>Potash	  133,745   128,933   156,633 Tonnes</p>
<p>Dry Bulk	 21,192	   0	   0 Tonnes</p>
<p>Liquid Bulk    28,091	   0    19,148 Tonnes</p>
<p>General Cargo   5,082	   0     5,674 Tonnes</p>
<p>Total	 1,094,614   990,252 1,250,350 Tonnes</p>
<p>VESSEL	  APRIL '97 APRIL '96 APRIL '95</p>
<p>Domestic	     46	  38	  51</p>
<p>Foreign		 7	   8	   8</p>
<p>American		1	   0	   1</p>
<p>Total		  54	  46	  60</p>
<p>N.B. All statistics for period of April 1 to 30.</p>
<p>((Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
